---
import ClubLayout from '../../../layouts/ClubLayout.astro';
---

<ClubLayout
  name="Cardiff City Jiu Jitsu Club"
  subtitle="Japanese Jiu Jitsu in Cardiff"
  description="Japanese Jiu Jitsu training for juniors and adults at Sport Wales National Centre in Cardiff, with class times, fees and contact details."
  when={['Wednesdays 7.00-8.30pm', 'Saturdays 5.30-7.00pm']}
  where="Sport Wales National Centre, Sophia Gardens, Cardiff CF11 9SW"
  contacts={[
    { label: 'Email', href: 'mailto:cardiffjitsuclub@gmail.com?subject=Jiu Jitsu enquiry' },
    { label: 'Join the WhatsApp enquiries group', href: 'https://chat.whatsapp.com/E5m8DtR2S4u6PTiQ9iDmkd?mode=gi_t', newTab: true },
    { label: 'Facebook', href: 'https://www.facebook.com/cardiffjitsu', newTab: true },
    { label: 'Instagram', href: 'https://www.instagram.com/cardiffjitsu/', newTab: true },
  ]}
>

  <p slot="intro" class="lead">
    Friendly, structured classes focused on practical self-defence, fitness,
    and progression. Beginners always welcome.
  </p>

  <!-- EMBEDS -->
  <div slot="after-details" class="grid" style="margin-top: 24px; margin-bottom: 24px;">

    <div class="card">
      <h2>Class Schedule</h2>
      <iframe title="Cardiff City training calendar" src="https://calendar.google.com/calendar/embed?height=600&wkst=2&ctz=Europe%2FLondon&showPrint=0&title=Cardiff%20Jitsu%20Club%20training%20times&hl=en_GB&showTz=0&showCalendars=0&showTabs=0&src=Y2FyZGlmZmppdHN1Y2x1YkBnbWFpbC5jb20&src=NzY2NDQyODMwZTgxN2I0N2MxMjg5ZTk0ZTI0NGYzN2ExNWE3YzQ3ZGMxNGVmMzI3MDAyOWJmZWE3MzNmMTM0ZkBncm91cC5jYWxlbmRhci5nb29nbGUuY29t&color=%23cc003c&color=%238E24AA"></iframe>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <h2>Location</h2>
      <iframe title="Sport Wales National Centre location" src="https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d2484.492274216916!2d-3.193130523034548!3d51.48583327180841!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x486e1ca6c0340f07%3A0xfc485e8a14d53c4!2sSport%20Wales%20National%20Centre!5e0!3m2!1sen!2suk!4v1743847898759!5m2!1sen!2suk"></iframe>
    </div>

  </div>

  <!-- TEXT SECTIONS -->
  <div slot="before-contact" class="grid">

    <div class="card">
      <h2>Your first session</h2>
      <p>
        Come along to one of our scheduled sessions, ideally 10 minutes early.
        There is no need to book in advance.
      </p>
      <p>
        We recommend joining the <a href="https://chat.whatsapp.com/E5m8DtR2S4u6PTiQ9iDmkd?mode=gi_t" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cardiff Jiu Jitsu enquiries WhatsApp group</a> before you come, where you can ask any questions.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <h2>Arriving at the dojo</h2>
      <p>
        When you enter the building, turn right at reception and go up the
        stairs, following the signs for the Judo Dojo.
      </p>
      <p>
        Bring a water bottle, or buy a refillable one from reception for about
        £2.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <h2>Costs and trial sessions</h2>
      <p>
        The club is not-for-profit and all instructors are volunteers. Your
        first two weeks are free. After that, the club subscription is
        £15/month and covers both the Wednesday and Saturday sessions.
        Discounts are available for multiple family members. You
        will also need a licence from our parent body, The Jiu Jitsu
        Foundation, which costs £38/year for adults and £24/year for juniors.
        There is no upfront payment during the first two weeks.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <h2>What should I wear?</h2>
      <p>
        For your first few sessions, wear tracksuit bottoms and a T-shirt. If
        you decide to continue, you will need a training suit,
        called a gi, which is usually cheaper to buy through the club. Please
        also bring flip-flops or sandals for when you are not on the mat.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <h2>Who can attend?</h2>
      <p>
        Children aged 6+ and adults are welcome. We have a large dojo and
        multiple instructors, so junior and adult sessions run side by side.
        You can learn Jiu Jitsu at the same time as your children.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <h2>What does training feel like?</h2>
      <p>
        Training involves contact, but it is cooperative rather than
        competitive. One person, or sometimes several people, plays the
        attacker while the other practises a technique demonstrated by the
        instructor, then you swap roles. At times, especially in gradings, you
        will work under pressure to test your abilities in realistic scenarios
        while keeping everyone safe.
      </p>
    </div>

  </div>

  <p>Cardiff City Jiu Jitsu Club is a member of <a href="https://www.jitsufoundation.org">The Jiu Jitsu Foundation</a>.</p>
</ClubLayout>
